# Paginated List + Search / Filter Patterns

> Methodology: `.agents/skills/integration-regression-review/SKILL.md` (Phase C2)  
> Functional QA: `.agents/skills/functional-verification-review/SKILL.md` (search + page matrix)  
> Hotwire/Turbo: `.cursor/rules/hotwire-integration-patterns.mdc`

**Core rule:** After any mutation or filter change, **page index**, **filtered result set**, and **URL query string** must stay consistent. Implement all three layers:

1. **Collection** — load `min(requested_page, total_pages)` or page 1 when empty  
2. **URL** — GET redirect or `history.replaceState` when page is corrected  
3. **UI outside frame** — total count, empty message, pagination links include filters  

---

## A. Page overflow (delete / empty page)

| ID | What breaks | Repro | Sev |
|----|-------------|-------|-----|
| **PAGE-OVERFLOW-01** | Delete last row(s) on last page → stay on `page=N`, empty list, no pagination | 10 rows, per=2, page 5, delete all on page | 🟠 |
| **PAGE-OVERFLOW-02** | `total_pages.zero?` early return leaves overflow empty collection | Delete every row in DB while on page 5 | 🟠 |
| **PAGE-GET-01** | `index` GET has no redirect when `page > total_pages` | GET `?page=99` | 🟠 |
| **PAGE-TURBO-01** | Turbo repage fixes data but URL still wrong → F5 breaks | Same as OVERFLOW-01 via turbo delete | 🟠 |
| **PAGE-EMPTY-01** | `pagination_nav` hidden when `blank?` masks overflow symptom | Empty page 5 with data on page 4 | 🟡 |

**Fix reference (two layers — both required):**

| Layer | GET (full page) | Turbo mutate (inline delete) |
|-------|-----------------|---------------------------|
| Collection | `repage` / clamp page | `repage_index_collection_if_overflow` → `fetch_index_page(last)` |
| URL | `redirect_to_last_page_if_overflow!` (303) | `history-replace` **only when** page was corrected (`repaged_to` present) |
| Filters | `index_list_url(q:, published:, page:)` single helper | Same helper in `history_replace_url_value` |

**ai-housemaker reference (house series `25da272`):**

```ruby
# repage returns effective page for URL sync, else nil
def repage_index_collection_if_overflow
  requested_page = Pagination::PageParam.coerce(params[:page], default: nil)
  return nil unless requested_page&.positive?
  return 1 if total_pages.zero?                    # PAGE-OVERFLOW-02 fix
  return nil if requested_page <= total_pages
  @house_series = fetch_index_page(total_pages)
  total_pages                                    # signal history-replace
end

# destroy: append history-replace only when repaged
streams << index_history_replace_stream(repaged_to) if repaged_to
```

**Still required if missing:** `index` GET → `redirect_to_last_page_if_overflow!` (properties has it; house series may still need — **PAGE-GET-01**).

